# U4-Production Department Guidelines

The U4-Production department focuses on web presence, operations, and production for cFish.io using WordPress.

## Department Role

- Lead web presence development through WordPress
- Manage UcWebZ operations and content production
- Develop and maintain WordPress themes and plugins
- Create custom WordPress functionality for client sites
- Implement cross-platform integration with other cFish.io platforms
- Align all implementations with the Produce (U4) philosophical principle

## Core Technologies

- **WordPress Core**: 6.0+ compatibility required
- **PHP**: 7.4+ compliance required
- **JavaScript**: Modern ES6+ implementation
- **CSS**: SASS/SCSS preprocessing recommended
- **Build Tools**: Webpack/Gulp for automation
- **Version Control**: Git with feature branch workflow

## WordPress Development Standards

- Follow [WordPress coding standards](https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/wordpress-coding-standards/)
- See detailed WordPress guidelines in [wp-development.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/wp-development.mdc)
- Use Object-Oriented Programming for all custom functionality
- Implement appropriate security practices throughout
- Create proper documentation for all components

## File Organization

- Follow UcF file organization patterns:
  - Store files in appropriate departmental directories
  - Use consistent naming: `ucf-[department].[function]-[description]-[date].[extension]`
  - Example: `ucf-u4.3-widget-registration-20250507.php`

- WordPress-specific organization:
  ```
  U4-Production/
    WordPress/
      themes/
        cfish-theme/
      plugins/
        cfish-core/
      functions/
      blocks/
  ```

## Philosophical Alignment

As Produce (U4) department, focus on:
- Productive output and efficient execution
- High-quality deliverables that meet client needs
- Consistent branding and user experience
- Optimized performance and loading times
- Cross-platform compatibility
- Sustainable maintenance practices

## Integration Requirements

- Create WordPress hooks for integration with other platforms:
  - ClickUp (cFish.App) - Task management integration
  - Notion (U.cFish.io) - Knowledge base integration
  - Vendasta (cFish.Vip) - Client solution integration

- Implement tYDiSync~ compatibility:
  - Add appropriate metadata for cross-platform synchronization
  - Create data transformation hooks for format conversion
  - Respect synchronization markers and protocols
  - Test synchronization across all platforms

## Relaunch Priorities

For the April 2025 relaunch, focus on:
- Knowledge monetization features as primary differentiators
- Documentation excellence as a marketable service offering
- Partnership enablement through robust APIs
- Mobile optimization for field operations
- Performance optimization for expected traffic increase 